# Admin Console Rules

This is the **identity platform operator console** — not `byte-forge-admin` (marketplace ops).

## Layout

- **Protected routes** use `(protected).tsx` sidebar shell (`AdminSidebar` + main content).
- **Auth routes** (`/login`, `/register`) use full-page centered card — no sidebar.
- `(auth).tsx` redirects authenticated users away from auth pages via `safeReturnTo(searchParams.returnTo)`.
- Nav items live in `~/config/admin-nav.ts` with `icon` + `match: "exact" | "prefix"`.
- Sidebar links use `AdminNavLink` (icon + label, active state).

## Auth

- API: `~/lib/api/admin-auth.api.ts` via BFF server `action()` calls.
- Clients API: `~/lib/api/clients.api.ts` via `fetcher` (session cookies + CSRF).
- Session: `~/lib/auth/session.ts` (`getSession`, `logoutAction`, `useSession`).
- `returnTo`: `~/lib/auth/return-to.ts` — allowlist `/`, `/users`, `/clients`, `/audit`.
- CSRF: `api-client.ts` sends `X-XSRF-TOKEN` from `xsrf-token` cookie on state-changing requests.
- Protected routes redirect unauthenticated users to `/login?returnTo=...`.

## Scope

- Users, OAuth clients, platform roles, audit — yes.
- Shops, products, orders, campaigns — no.

Do not duplicate end-user self-registration from `aponika-auth-frontend`.
